al or a sharply shifted national environment could tighten the race, but no current evidence suggests either.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Chellie Pingree (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Chellie Pingree is seeking a tenth term in a southern Maine district that leans Democratic by about eleven points. Her Republican challenger, Army veteran Ron Russell, won his primary in June and has campaigned through a series of fall debates and candidate forums. Local coverage has been routine, with no sign of a competitive dynamic emerging.\n\nA University of New Hampshire poll of likely voters in late September showed Pingree ahead 57 to 35. Fundraising strongly favors the incumbent, who holds a large cash advantage over Russell's roughly eight thousand dollars on hand. Prediction markets price a Pingree win at about 96 percent. With the district's lean, her incumbency, the polling, and the money all pointing the same direction, the seat remains firmly in the Democratic column heading into November.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.989, "margin": 20.81}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9938, "margin": 20.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9879, "margin": 20.9}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9957, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9949, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9948, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9951, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 21.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9926, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9947, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9955, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9935, "margin": 20.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_de